# addressed (id|relay-url), not bare ids, per AGENTS.md's mesh-join gotcha
# (bare-id seeds left three prior nodes invisible fleet-wide despite
# healthz=200) -- seeded from va/sj/bkk's own real ids + relay URLs.
# RELAY URL FORM MATTERS (bn-relay-front-native-dial-timeout): the standalone
# iroh-relay on bkk/va/sj runs TLS, which moves EVERY relay service
# (/relay websocket, /ping net_report probe, QAD) to the https socket :3343;
# the plaintext :3340 listener is captive-portal-only (verified live
# 2026-08-04: ws://:3340/relay -> 404, :3340/ping -> 404, QAD cert is
# *.relay.shadw.app so IP-literal URLs fail it too). http://<ip>:3340 entries
# are therefore dead relays: never probed-preferred, never dialable. Name
# the https :3343 hostnames (cert is the *.relay.shadw.app wildcard, so the
# DNS name is mandatory -- an IP literal fails TLS verification).
